# Production bar

A task/module is not done until:

- Acceptance criteria covered (happy, fail, edge) with tests or explicit verified manual checks when UI-only
- Error, empty, and loading states handled where the UI/API surface needs them
- No placeholder secrets; no `TODO` left as the only path for a claimed feature
- Security/authz considered for the change (delegate to m4trix-security when sensitive)
- Relevant docs in `docs/sdlc/` updated
- For UI: uses the project design system / theme — no one-off colors/typography unless approved
- Code craft satisfied (`04-code-craft`): think → simple → surgical → verified; reuse where warranted
- Verifier checklist passed (m4trix-verifier); no false “tests passed”
- Delivery voice (`05-delivery-voice`): no IDE/AI-editor attribution in product docs, commits, or PRs

Mockups, stubs, and “wire it later” are backlog items — not done.
